# Lint After Every Change

After any code modification, bug fix, refactor, schema change, or feature addition:

1. Run `pnpm run lint` before reporting the task complete.
2. Fix lint errors introduced by the change.
3. Re-run `pnpm run lint` until it passes, or report remaining failures honestly.
4. Never claim lint passed unless the command was actually executed in this session.

Also run relevant tests and `pnpm typecheck` when those scripts exist and the change warrants them — but **lint is mandatory every time**.

Use the `verify-changes` skill for the full post-change checklist.
